      "round_summary": "Round 1/3: Fix DUT bug causing `leaf_request_propagates_to_top` assertion failure. Error category: dut_bug. Root cause: In `arbitCell.io.xr` combinational logic (arbit.scala:83), the condition `!holdToken` prevented the top cell (`C0`, `holdToken=1` initially) from propagating leaf requests upward to `sr`, which remained `idle` while all leaves requested. Fix: Changed condition on line 83 from `!holdToken` to `(!holdToken || io.topCell)`, allowing the top cell to always combinationaly propagate requests regardless of `holdToken` state. This directly addresses the causal path: the top cell has no parent to wait for, so `holdToken` should not gate upward request propagation at the top. The assertion label `leaf_request_propagates_to_top` is preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions exist for this DUT logic pattern.",
